I've just been having some most excellent fun with a pet chameleon.
They really are brilliant, switching from really useful priest-eating
Vampire Lords to harmless newts to tunnel-munchingrock moles to god-
only-knows-whatses every few turns. Especially effective in slashem,
where kamikaze attacks just revert the shapechanger back to its own
form, rather than killing it outright.

Anyway, one of its many forms was a rabid wolf, which got me thinking
- shouldn't tame and peaceful rabid monsters be a little more
unreliable than normal monsters? Perhaps prone to bouts of confusion
that can cause them to bite the PC and fellow pets..?


